# .vercelignore -- controls what the Vercel CLI uploads on `vercel deploy`.
#
# The CLI does NOT read .gitignore. Anything not excluded here is uploaded
# into the deployment source archive, gitignored secrets included. Confirmed
# on 2026-09-03 by inspecting a live production deployment: it shipped the
# project's local .env files and agent tool directories.
#
# Neither DenScope nor Ayni has a Git integration on Vercel, so every deploy
# is a CLI upload from a working directory. This file is the only guard.

# Root-level dot entries only.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. An unanchored `.*` also matches dot
# components nested inside a path: on 2026-09-03 it silently dropped
# src/app/.well-known/x402/ from a production build, and the route 404'd
# until this was fixed. Do not remove the slash.
#
# Nothing dot-prefixed at the repo root is needed to build these projects on
# Vercel: env vars come from the project settings, and the real build configs
# (next.config.ts, eslint.config.mjs, tsconfig.json, package.json) are not
# dotfiles. One rule covers .env*, local key material and the agent tool
# directories (.claude/, .cursor/, .superpowers/, ...) without a list that
# goes stale every time a new tool is installed.
/.*

# Build output and caches -- rebuilt remotely.
node_modules
test-results
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
